# variant_match — `branch ifVariant VALUE VARIANT goto L` narrows a payloadless
# enum by discriminant (README ss10.5/ss13). Builds Status.done and matches it,
# printing "is done". (todos WS1-063)

VariantMatch is project
VariantMatch module examplesVariantMatch
VariantMatch target console
VariantMatch entry main

examplesVariantMatch is module
examplesVariantMatch path examples.variantMatch
examplesVariantMatch exports main
examplesVariantMatch purpose "Match an enum value with ifVariant"
examplesVariantMatch invariant "Takes the done path only when the value is the done variant"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

Status is enum
Status variant open
Status variant done
Status purpose "Lifecycle state of a task"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Build a done Status and branch on it with ifVariant"
main invariant "Prints 'is done' when the value matches the done variant"
main let doneText immutable String "is done"
main let openText immutable String "still open"
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main do makeStatus
main branch ifVariant currentStatus done goto isDone
main do writeOpen
main return okCode
main at isDone do writeDone
main return okCode

makeStatus is call
makeStatus in main
makeStatus invokes Status.done
makeStatus out currentStatus Status

writeDone is call
writeDone in main
writeDone invokes console.writeLine
writeDone arg text String doneText

writeOpen is call
writeOpen in main
writeOpen invokes console.writeLine
writeOpen arg text String openText
